WEBVTT

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.171
It's morning. Wake up!
It's morning. Wake up!

00:01:31.171 --> 00:01:33.407
It's morning. Wake up!

00:01:33.407 --> 00:01:37.477
It's morning. Wake up!
It's morning. Wake up!

00:01:37.477 --> 00:01:39.604
It's morning. Wake up!

00:02:07.441 --> 00:02:12.845
Mihoshi, my partner, it's already
been a month since you died.

00:02:14.181 --> 00:02:17.617
You were always such a burden to me.

00:02:17.617 --> 00:02:20.187
But now I will never see you again,

00:02:20.187 --> 00:02:24.817
and that knowledge makes
me so happy, I can't tell you!

00:02:28.695 --> 00:02:32.999
May your soul rest in peace, Mihoshi!

00:02:32.999 --> 00:02:35.535
What? Mihoshi is alive?

00:02:35.535 --> 00:02:39.406
Now, all I just said was
it's possible she was alive.

00:02:39.406 --> 00:02:42.209
But I thought Mihoshi had died

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:45.045
in the line of duty while
pursuing the wanted criminal Ryoko!

00:02:45.045 --> 00:02:50.050
Well, that post in the solar system
has been vacant for quite some time.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:52.985
So they haven't really
followed up the case yet, you see.

00:02:54.221 --> 00:02:57.591
Detective Kiyone, here's the thing.

00:02:57.591 --> 00:03:00.894
Since you were Detective
First Class Mihoshi's partner,

00:03:00.894 --> 00:03:04.531
I would like you to undertake
a search for her immediately.

00:03:04.531 --> 00:03:06.089
That's an order.

00:03:08.768 --> 00:03:11.371
I don't believe it!

00:03:11.371 --> 00:03:15.542
And here I thought my
nightmare was over once and for all.

00:03:15.542 --> 00:03:18.445
Oh, God!

00:03:18.445 --> 00:03:22.176
Please, please don't let Mihoshi be alive!

00:03:38.865 --> 00:03:41.595
It feels so nice.

00:03:49.342 --> 00:03:52.539
Just another quiet day.

00:03:58.818 --> 00:04:03.881
For some reason, this peaceful
atmosphere makes me sleepy.

00:04:19.906 --> 00:04:23.543
Thanks for waiting! And it's
just the way you wanted it!

00:04:23.543 --> 00:04:24.911
All right. We are ready for this.

00:04:24.911 --> 00:04:27.781
Thanks for going to all this trouble.

00:04:27.781 --> 00:04:29.849
Hey, what's going on now?

00:04:29.849 --> 00:04:31.817
We've got a new bath now, right?

00:04:32.919 --> 00:04:36.323
What do you mean? There
already was a bathroom there.

00:04:36.323 --> 00:04:42.429
Well, we asked Washu to
remodel the interior just a bit.

00:04:42.429 --> 00:04:46.433
Well, is Washu good at construction as well?

00:04:46.433 --> 00:04:49.925
But you guys should have asked us
if it's okay to change the bathroom.

00:04:51.237 --> 00:04:54.934
Whoa! This looks pretty cool.

00:05:00.113 --> 00:05:01.948
What in the world is this?

00:05:01.948 --> 00:05:05.552
I connected the inside of the
bathroom to a different dimension.

00:05:05.552 --> 00:05:10.056
Like when I created my research lab
in the storage unit... same technique.

00:05:10.056 --> 00:05:13.193
Enough with creating
dimensions all over the house!

00:05:13.193 --> 00:05:16.963
Tenchi! You shouldn't be so narrow-minded.

00:05:16.963 --> 00:05:21.635
The bath will serve as a way of bringing
our whole group closer together.

00:05:21.635 --> 00:05:26.573
Everyone, I think we should
really get close to each other now.

00:05:26.573 --> 00:05:29.609
But this one is the ladies' bath.

00:05:29.609 --> 00:05:32.646
You two should go to the men's bath.

00:05:32.646 --> 00:05:35.315
- It's right this way. There.
- Well, ah, but, men's bath?

00:05:35.315 --> 00:05:36.783
- It's right this way. There.
- But there's only one bath in here, right?

00:05:36.783 --> 00:05:37.751
- But there's only one bath in here, right?

00:05:37.751 --> 00:05:39.352
- Bye.
- But there's only one bath in here, right?

00:05:39.352 --> 00:05:40.842
Huh?

00:05:42.122 --> 00:05:44.920
Well then, we should go in there.

00:05:47.293 --> 00:05:48.995
What do you think you're doing?

00:05:48.995 --> 00:05:51.464
Hey, all I'm saying is
closeness in a family is important,

00:05:51.464 --> 00:05:54.634
and so is a good bath.

00:05:54.634 --> 00:05:57.603
What the heck are you thinking?

00:05:58.204 --> 00:06:00.206
Anyway, let go of my shirt!

00:06:00.206 --> 00:06:03.276
- I'm not letting go.
- Come on. Whose side are you on?

00:06:03.276 --> 00:06:06.112
Those girls are inside there.
Don't you understand?

00:06:06.112 --> 00:06:07.981
That's exactly why I'm peeping.

00:06:07.981 --> 00:06:10.517
Aha! You just want to peep, don't you?

00:06:10.517 --> 00:06:12.542
Let me go!

00:06:13.186 --> 00:06:14.654
I'm coming in.

00:06:14.654 --> 00:06:15.655
What?

00:06:15.655 --> 00:06:17.190
What is this?

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:19.488
It's just the same old bathroom.

00:06:20.627 --> 00:06:22.652
Now, this is really strange.

00:06:24.564 --> 00:06:26.466
Oh, hi. I forgot to tell you this.

00:06:26.466 --> 00:06:30.402
When the door is opened by a man,
it doesn't lead to another dimension.

00:06:32.639 --> 00:06:35.809
I wouldn't mind bathing with you.

00:06:35.809 --> 00:06:38.445
So, don't you want to go inside with me?

00:06:38.445 --> 00:06:41.247
Well, what do you say, Tenchi?

00:06:41.247 --> 00:06:43.917
Get back in here! That's enough!

00:06:43.917 --> 00:06:47.318
Ouch! You don't have
to yank me so hard.

00:07:11.411 --> 00:07:14.080
The house must be just ahead of me.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:15.945
That's what the coordinates are.

00:07:20.954 --> 00:07:22.387
That must be it.

00:07:29.028 --> 00:07:31.431
I don't know what to do with Dad.

00:07:31.431 --> 00:07:34.601
You there, excuse me.

00:07:34.601 --> 00:07:35.602
Hello.

00:07:35.602 --> 00:07:38.264
I want to ask you something.

00:07:38.872 --> 00:07:41.067
What can I do for you?

00:07:44.511 --> 00:07:46.412
Have you ever seen this woman before?

00:07:46.412 --> 00:07:47.313
Huh?

00:07:47.313 --> 00:07:48.982
Sure. I know her.

00:07:48.982 --> 00:07:50.472
What?

00:07:51.618 --> 00:07:54.254
Do you know where she
is now? Tell me! Tell me!

00:07:54.254 --> 00:07:56.347
Okay! She's right over there.

00:08:03.029 --> 00:08:04.597
That's it.

00:08:04.597 --> 00:08:07.828
My all-too-brief peaceful
moments are over now.

00:08:08.802 --> 00:08:11.638
Hey, hold still. I'm trying to dry you off.

00:08:11.638 --> 00:08:14.407
Yes, that was a nice bath.

00:08:14.407 --> 00:08:16.810
Yes, that certainly was.

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:19.245
What say we take another one later?

00:08:19.245 --> 00:08:20.446
Excellent idea.

00:08:20.446 --> 00:08:24.384
Wow, Kiyone! I missed you.

00:08:24.384 --> 00:08:25.485
Huh?

00:08:25.485 --> 00:08:28.888
It's been so many days,
but I knew you'd come for me.

00:08:28.888 --> 00:08:30.957
How many days has it been, anyway?

00:08:30.957 --> 00:08:34.294
Do you know I couldn't sleep at
night because I missed you so much?

00:08:34.294 --> 00:08:36.196
So you sleep during the daytime, huh?

00:08:36.196 --> 00:08:38.031
Well, well, you must be tired.

00:08:38.031 --> 00:08:42.869
You've come all the way
to find your partner Mihoshi.

00:08:42.869 --> 00:08:46.239
You must have been worried about her.

00:08:46.239 --> 00:08:50.910
To see Mihoshi alive and
well makes me so very mad.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:53.813
I mean, makes me so very glad.

00:08:53.813 --> 00:08:57.517
We have a special chemistry between us.

00:08:57.517 --> 00:08:59.352
And together, we were
so competent, she and I.

00:08:59.352 --> 00:09:03.482
Good friendships between two
women are a beautiful thing indeed.

00:09:05.391 --> 00:09:08.795
It seems like you've been taking
very good care of Mihoshi here.

00:09:08.795 --> 00:09:12.065
That's right. Everybody here is so nice.

00:09:12.065 --> 00:09:14.334
Oh, let me introduce them to you.

00:09:14.334 --> 00:09:18.037
- This is Tenchi Masaki.
- We've met, kind of.

00:09:18.037 --> 00:09:22.406
- And this is his father, Nobuyuki.
- Hi, nice to meet you.

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:27.213
And that's the grandfather, Katsuhito.

00:09:27.213 --> 00:09:29.549
It is a pleasure to meet you.

00:09:29.549 --> 00:09:34.320
This is the space pirate, Ryoko.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.584
Hi. How ya doin'?

00:09:38.491 --> 00:09:43.596
Now, what in the universe is the most
wanted criminal doing here with you?

00:09:43.596 --> 00:09:47.200
- Well, just seems kind of natural.
- Kind of natural?

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:49.168
Move on with the introductions, will ya?

00:09:49.168 --> 00:09:50.303
Think I will.

00:09:50.303 --> 00:09:54.340
Next to Ryoko is Ayeka from the planet Jurai.

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:56.240
Hello. How do you do?

00:09:57.477 --> 00:09:59.379
You mean Princess Ayeka who's been missing?

00:09:59.379 --> 00:10:03.216
- And next to her is Sasami.
- Hi. How are you?

00:10:03.216 --> 00:10:06.452
Princess Sasami? How did
the two of them end up here?

00:10:06.452 --> 00:10:10.056
And this is the genius
scientist Washu, of course.

00:10:10.056 --> 00:10:11.819
Huh?!

00:10:14.961 --> 00:10:19.227
Y-You mean to tell me she's
that legendary mad scientist?

00:10:20.433 --> 00:10:22.936
She has to make such a
big deal out of everything?

00:10:22.936 --> 00:10:26.372
I have to say I think her
reaction is quite normal.

00:10:26.372 --> 00:10:29.509
How did all these people
come to meet one another?

00:10:29.509 --> 00:10:31.744
What is going on here?

00:10:31.744 --> 00:10:36.807
All I can say is things just
seemed to develop this way.

00:10:42.155 --> 00:10:43.723
Damn!

00:10:43.723 --> 00:10:45.425
Space pirate Ryoko!

00:10:45.425 --> 00:10:47.860
I hereby place you under arrest.

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:50.522
I see. You're not kidding, are you?

00:11:07.347 --> 00:11:09.949
These croquettes are delicious!

00:11:09.949 --> 00:11:13.553
The ratio between the potatoes
and the ground meat is just perfect.

00:11:13.553 --> 00:11:17.156
This could stand up
under any scientific analysis.

00:11:17.156 --> 00:11:20.293
And Sasami cooked all
this fine food, is that right?

00:11:20.293 --> 00:11:23.456
That's right. You really
are a great cook, Sasami.

00:11:24.464 --> 00:11:27.200
Hard to believe Sasami is related to Ayeka.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:28.801
That's none of your concern.

00:11:28.801 --> 00:11:30.370
Here, Kiyone.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:32.171
Have some more if you're still hungry.

00:11:32.171 --> 00:11:35.038
Oh, wow. Thanks. I am.

00:11:36.142 --> 00:11:39.737
You eat like a horse, Kiyone. You know that?

00:11:40.747 --> 00:11:43.416
The one who eats like a horse is you.

00:11:43.416 --> 00:11:46.283
Yeah, I guess I am that way.

00:11:56.029 --> 00:11:58.264
What's going on here?

00:11:58.264 --> 00:12:00.566
What happened to the scene I was just in?

00:12:00.566 --> 00:12:03.436
What am I doing here eating
lunch with these people?

00:12:03.436 --> 00:12:06.873
Well, for one thing, it's
lunch time. We can't help that.

00:12:06.873 --> 00:12:08.307
Mihoshi!

00:12:08.307 --> 00:12:11.003
Boy, she really is serious.

00:12:12.045 --> 00:12:14.847
Now, don't make it difficult for me.

00:12:14.847 --> 00:12:17.083
Hold on a minute.

00:12:17.083 --> 00:12:18.985
I'm in the middle of eating here.

00:12:18.985 --> 00:12:20.253
Come on, Mihoshi.

00:12:20.253 --> 00:12:26.959
Wait. Okay, so Ryoko is a vicious pirate
and one of the worst criminals ever.

00:12:26.959 --> 00:12:29.562
But on the other hand,
in her behalf I have to say,

00:12:29.562 --> 00:12:31.631
she did give me the
bigger rice cake the other day.

00:12:31.631 --> 00:12:33.766
What do you mean?

00:12:33.766 --> 00:12:37.167
Mihoshi, you've got to think before you talk.

00:12:38.337 --> 00:12:40.907
And just which side are you on anyway?

00:12:40.907 --> 00:12:47.880
Kiyone, may I say you are
truly the paragon of detectives.

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:49.882
I would like to assist you

00:12:49.882 --> 00:12:53.086
in arresting this most vicious
pirate and wanted criminal.

00:12:53.086 --> 00:12:54.487
You little traitor.

00:12:54.487 --> 00:12:56.956
What are you talking about, Ryoko?

00:12:56.956 --> 00:13:00.493
I never was on your side
to begin with. You know that.

00:13:00.493 --> 00:13:05.624
Ayeka, you think you're going to be
rid of me once I'm arrested, is that it?

00:13:07.233 --> 00:13:09.268
I have no idea what you are talking about.

00:13:09.268 --> 00:13:12.939
I am just trying to cooperate with the police.

00:13:12.939 --> 00:13:15.641
Yeah, well, you're not gonna get your way.

00:13:15.641 --> 00:13:18.111
Mihoshi, some tea.

00:13:18.111 --> 00:13:20.279
Okay!

00:13:20.279 --> 00:13:23.583
Look at you! You call yourself a detective?

00:13:23.583 --> 00:13:26.347
Sorry. I'm just polite.

00:13:27.353 --> 00:13:30.584
Wait right here. I'll be
done with her in a minute.

00:13:33.025 --> 00:13:36.085
That's it, girl. Step outside.

00:14:07.994 --> 00:14:09.859
That's something.

00:14:14.133 --> 00:14:15.760
Yagami!

00:14:42.128 --> 00:14:46.232
Mihoshi, why don't you use that?

00:14:46.232 --> 00:14:48.097
All right!

00:14:49.068 --> 00:14:51.137
I am a space detective.

00:14:51.137 --> 00:14:54.868
Fighting till death is
what I do. That's what I am.

00:14:55.575 --> 00:14:57.372
Here I go!

00:14:59.579 --> 00:15:01.414
Whoa! Yipes!

00:15:01.414 --> 00:15:03.780
Oh, boy! Whoa!

00:15:10.623 --> 00:15:12.124
Oh, boy.

00:15:12.124 --> 00:15:14.718
Well, that's Mihoshi for ya.

00:15:17.463 --> 00:15:19.665
It's gotta be kidding!

00:15:19.665 --> 00:15:24.370
I gotta tell you something.
Your partner really cracks me up.

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:27.134
I'm not that easy!

00:15:32.311 --> 00:15:33.938
Pretty good.

00:15:35.881 --> 00:15:37.610
But not good enough.

00:15:48.361 --> 00:15:50.192
You're mine!

00:15:55.234 --> 00:15:57.168
Whoa! A magical force field?

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:03.109
Azaka, Kamidake!

00:16:03.109 --> 00:16:06.145
Hold Ryoko tight and
do not let her get away.

00:16:06.145 --> 00:16:07.271
Yes, Ma'am.

00:16:14.487 --> 00:16:16.756
Y-You jerks!

00:16:16.756 --> 00:16:19.458
We are sorry about this...

00:16:19.458 --> 00:16:21.260
...but we have to obey
Princess Ayeka's orders.

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:23.091
Damn!

00:16:25.231 --> 00:16:27.667
I think I got you now.

00:16:27.667 --> 00:16:31.404
Finally, the notorious criminal goes to jail.

00:16:31.404 --> 00:16:35.374
Ryoko, I guess I'll
visit you in jail. I promise.

00:16:35.374 --> 00:16:37.376
And I'll write to you.

00:16:37.376 --> 00:16:41.113
Hey, I'm still here. Stop talking like that.

00:16:41.113 --> 00:16:42.615
You take it from here.

00:16:42.615 --> 00:16:44.105
Okay.

00:16:48.988 --> 00:16:56.128
You are charged under Galaxy
Police law item 2546, amendment 973.

00:16:56.128 --> 00:17:00.199
The suspect has the right to remain silent
regarding issues to your disadvantage.

00:17:00.199 --> 00:17:02.497
You also have the right to an attorney.

00:17:07.506 --> 00:17:12.500
Get out of my way! Get out of my way!

00:17:23.255 --> 00:17:29.228
Everything was going so smoothly
until they made Mihoshi my partner again.

00:17:29.228 --> 00:17:32.531
Since then, it's been a nightmare.

00:17:32.531 --> 00:17:34.834
I know.

00:17:34.834 --> 00:17:37.302
Well, here, have some <i>sake.</i>

00:17:38.704 --> 00:17:42.003
Ohhh, nice drinking!

00:17:43.809 --> 00:17:46.979
Then we were demoted
and assigned to a remote site,

00:17:46.979 --> 00:17:50.312
losing all chance of promotion
to the higher ranks at headquarters.

00:17:52.084 --> 00:17:55.520
All that was Mihoshi's fault.
It's all because of her!

00:18:08.934 --> 00:18:10.424
Kiyone.

00:18:14.006 --> 00:18:16.776
As per your request,
I contacted the planet Jurai

00:18:16.776 --> 00:18:19.845
and told them that you were on vacation.

00:18:19.845 --> 00:18:22.181
Is that really all right with you?

00:18:22.181 --> 00:18:23.716
Yes, thank you, Kiyone.

00:18:23.716 --> 00:18:27.153
We need a break in
some remote place, I think.

00:18:27.153 --> 00:18:30.623
- Right, Sasami?
- Mm-hmm.

00:18:30.623 --> 00:18:32.989
Well, then, we'll prepare for takeoff.

00:18:44.270 --> 00:18:46.864
Everybody, thank you for everything.

00:18:47.973 --> 00:18:51.911
I'll never forget you all.

00:18:51.911 --> 00:18:56.245
That's so sweet, and I will
always remember you, Mihoshi.

00:19:04.223 --> 00:19:06.292
So long, Mihoshi.

00:19:06.292 --> 00:19:09.693
I'm not gonna be able to visit
you or anything, but take care.

00:19:12.898 --> 00:19:14.934
Here.

00:19:14.934 --> 00:19:16.235
Some nice rice balls.

00:19:16.235 --> 00:19:19.338
Have some when you're
hungry on the way back home.

00:19:19.338 --> 00:19:22.741
Here. Take them with you.

00:19:22.741 --> 00:19:25.244
Thank you so much.

00:19:25.244 --> 00:19:27.974
Everybody, good-bye now.

00:19:29.748 --> 00:19:30.916
Good-bye!

00:19:30.916 --> 00:19:33.043
- Take care.
- Keep in touch.

00:19:34.987 --> 00:19:38.616
Good-bye! Good-bye.

00:19:47.766 --> 00:19:50.236
So, are you ready to go home?

00:19:50.236 --> 00:19:51.804
Yes.

00:19:51.804 --> 00:19:55.240
Looks like we're receiving
an ultra-space communication.

00:19:57.042 --> 00:19:58.310
Section Chief?

00:19:58.310 --> 00:20:05.251
As I reported, I've located Detective Mihoshi,
and we're heading back immediately.

00:20:05.251 --> 00:20:07.553
You don't need to do that.

00:20:07.553 --> 00:20:08.621
What?

00:20:08.621 --> 00:20:12.424
You have just received an appointment
from the chief of the Galaxy Police.

00:20:12.424 --> 00:20:13.914
Listen.

00:20:15.127 --> 00:20:18.898
As of today, Mihoshi and
Kiyone are assigned to Earth

00:20:18.898 --> 00:20:23.235
as officers in charge
of the solar system area.

00:20:23.235 --> 00:20:25.337
That's all.

00:20:25.337 --> 00:20:27.172
This can't be true!

00:20:27.172 --> 00:20:31.610
The personnel section chief was
very happy we found qualified officers.

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:33.669
Keep up your good work.

00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:37.550
Wow! This is great! I'm so happy.

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:39.785
Now we can stay on Earth!

00:20:39.785 --> 00:20:41.654
Aren't you happy, Kiyone?

00:20:41.654 --> 00:20:44.384
We get to work closely together again.

00:20:45.291 --> 00:20:48.961
We are still stationed on Earth!

00:20:48.961 --> 00:20:54.033
- Lucky! Lucky! Cha-cha-cha! Hooray!
- It's over.

00:20:54.033 --> 00:20:55.401
I am so happy!

00:20:55.401 --> 00:20:58.504
My career is in the toilet.

00:20:58.504 --> 00:21:02.031
I am so happy! I am so happy!

00:22:56.989 --> 00:23:01.026
In our next episode, Kiyone and
Mihoshi settle down as roommates

00:23:01.026 --> 00:23:03.996
in a tiny studio apartment
in an old building facing west.

00:23:03.996 --> 00:23:06.331
We'll be fried in this afternoon sun!

00:23:06.331 --> 00:23:08.434
Unable to keep up with the
high cost of living on Earth,

00:23:08.434 --> 00:23:10.469
they work day and night on part-time jobs.

00:23:10.469 --> 00:23:14.073
And whenever they receive a duty
call, fly out to space in the Yagami.

00:23:14.073 --> 00:23:16.775
Hang on, residents of the solar system.

00:23:16.775 --> 00:23:18.844
Next episode is:
"No Need for Resident Officers!"

00:23:18.844 --> 00:23:21.108
It's unquestionably pathetic.
